      "claim": "The approximate absolute temperatures of the four options are: (A) wax at room temperature ≈ 293 K, (B) water in ice water ≈ 273 K, (C) steam from coffee ≈ 373 K, (D) ice cube in tea ≈ 273 K.",
      "evidence": "Room temperature ≈ 20 °C = 293 K; ice–water equilibrium at 0 °C = 273 K; boiling water/steam ≈ 100 °C = 373 K; an ice cube immersed in tea remains at 0 °C while it exists.",
